From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nebel <nebel@localhost>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(manager): whitelist Nebel RP6 paddles virtual pad

The Retroid Pocket 6 routes its back paddles through gpio-keys (BTN_C/BTN_Z),
not through the gamepad MCU. nebel-gpio-keys grabs that node and re-emits the
paddles on a virtual uinput gamepad node "Nebel RP6 Paddles" (Nebel uinput
ids 0x222A:0x0004), matched as an extra gamepad source of the AYN composite
by the image's 02-ayn-controller.yaml; ayn_mcu translates BTN_C/BTN_Z into
Deck RightPaddle1/LeftPaddle1 (R4/L4 in Steam).

The node lives under /devices/virtual/input, so Manager discards it as
virtual before configs can claim it ("is virtual, skipping consideration").
Like "Nebel Trackpad Screen" in 0004, it is virtual by construction and
explicitly meant to be managed - add it to VIRT_DEVICE_WHITELIST.
---
 src/input/manager.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/src/input/manager.rs
+++ b/src/input/manager.rs
@@ -68,6 +68,11 @@
     // 01-retroid-controller.yaml. It is virtual but explicitly created by us
     // to be managed by InputPlumber.
     "Nebel Trackpad Screen",
+    // NebelOS: RP6 back paddles, re-emitted by nebel-gpio-keys from the
+    // hidden gpio-keys node (BTN_C/BTN_Z) so they can join the AYN composite
+    // as Deck R4/L4. Virtual by construction, explicitly meant to be
+    // managed.
+    "Nebel RP6 Paddles",
 ];
 
 #[derive(Error, Debug)]
